From: qlattice CPS darwin port (task-57)
Subject: [PATCH] pt_force.C: replace <malloc.h> with <stdlib.h> (macOS has no malloc.h)

The pinned CPS revision includes the glibc-only <malloc.h> in
cps_pp/src/util/parallel_transport/pt_base/qmp/pt_force.C (line 9).  That
directory has no explicit source list in its Makefile, so Makefile.rules'
wildcard picks the file up and the mac brew build compiles it (the nix build
compiles it too, but glibc provides <malloc.h> there).  macOS/BSD libc has no
<malloc.h>, so the mac build fails with:

  pt_force.C:9:10: fatal error: 'malloc.h' file not found

The file only needs standard declarations (it allocates through pt_amalloc()
from the parallel-transport headers; the earlier includes already bring in the
C++ standard library), so <stdlib.h> is the portable replacement; Linux
behaviour is unchanged (malloc/free declarations are the same).

--- a/cps_pp/src/util/parallel_transport/pt_base/qmp/pt_force.C
+++ b/cps_pp/src/util/parallel_transport/pt_base/qmp/pt_force.C
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 */
 
 #include <string.h>
-#include <malloc.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #include "asq_data_types.h"
 #include "pt_int.h"
 
